From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: own the Iris33 firmware mmap through the DMA API

Allocate one complete UC region for queues, SFR and the version1 mmap.
Map named AON, fence and timer resources through the DMA API. Retain all
mappings until PAS ownership is released, unwind partial maps in reverse
order and reject invalid ranges before any firmware boot command.

Use the existing DMA mask and a translated DMA domain. The firmware's
single device-region interval must contain only the three MMIO pages;
reject allocator holes, aliases and overlap with the shared DMA region.
Populate the reference version1 fields with explicit little-endian words.
Keep metadata immutable while PAS may own it and verify it before boot.
Other platforms retain their existing queue allocation and callback path.

Protocol reference: OnePlus SM7675 modules/DT
1138e00fee63582a0cc6a53af3286621786827b7, Qualcomm GPL-2.0-only
vidc/src/venus_hfi_queue.c and variant/iris33/src/msm_vidc_iris33.c.
Uke OEM DT 94c84aeb and current upstream f47d2236 are compared separately.
No fixed physical address, Android IOVA, DMA-mask widening, firmware or DT
match is added. Native resource binding, split pixel DMA and removal still
require separate implementation and qualification before activation.

